  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 102.06 Actively manage",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 102.06 “Actively manage” means to handle a waste or material, including waste-derived products and recyclable materials, in a controlled manner without causing:\n\n(a) A nuisance;\n\n(b) An adverse effect to the environment, public health and safety;\n\n(c) Accumulations which have no identifiable destination or value; and\n\n(d) A loss of material value in the market place due to material damage, degradation, or contamination.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 102.04) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
